diff --git a/FASTEST-PATH-Codex-2026-09-10.md b/FASTEST-PATH-Codex-2026-09-10.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9a092f2aba9fa1f7b45c2c0f49bdc3c3bd5337ed
--- /dev/null
+++ b/FASTEST-PATH-Codex-2026-09-10.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`
+
+**Do not fund the 200-worker-hour panel yet. No decision object has demonstrated three substantial learned contributions. Universal impossibility is also not established.**
+
+1. **Best candidate: joint user assignment, beam occupancy/activation, and power/mode decisions, before the classical search consumes the opportunity.** Let the per-user routes supply immediate and continuation values, and the set route correct their joint consequences. Association alone remains unresolved; fixed-assignment power/mode control has not shown substantial room for all three. Beating classical search is not a requirement or a gate.
+
+2. **The set route is not restricted to cross-beam interference.** A per-beam rule already sees an entire beam's users; a sum of per-user terms need not capture shared activation costs, occupancy thresholds, or simultaneous moves. Therefore the fast look's 2.1% does **not** bound this residual. Today's target-design report finds large residual corrections, including cancellation of exaggerated singleton sums. That establishes neither useful decisions nor learnability, but it defeats the assertion that the residual is intrinsically tiny. Joint association/control is a plausible arrangement to test, not a promised success.
+
+3. **Dispatch `ORACLE-RESIDUAL-TOGGLE` now: no training, two workers, eight preselected cached anchors under corrected physics.** Before the exact-search prefix, build one bounded candidate catalogue containing the incumbent, singleton moves, shared-beam bundles/evacuations, and coarse joint power/mode alternatives. Compare **exact summed per-user terms** with **those identical terms plus the exact set residual**; hold candidate coverage, observations, service constraints, and tie-breaking fixed. Use objective-aligned 48-boundary evaluation and pooled totals, with a common ratio optimization across anchors—not the old fixed-price snapshot. Report demand-capped bits/joule alongside capacity, and save controls and per-user delivery records.
+
+   The decisive number is the pooled-efficiency gain from enabling the residual, **not its prediction error or magnitude**. Use 10% as an explicit planning screen for “substantial.” A large gain establishes an opportunity worth learning; a small gain stops this candidate design, not every conceivable arrangement. No small bounded search can honestly prove universal impossibility. If it passes, run the smallest paired **FULL versus each of the three neutral-source DROP arms**, retaining and training every head, on held-out worlds. All three must deliver substantial gains; the oracle screen alone cannot establish that.
+
+4. **Pause the 9,000-epoch trajectory and repeated panel evaluations at the next saved checkpoint; stop panel expansion and the duplicate harness audit.** Retain one focused check of the source contrast. Fold the separate association/control searches into the residual experiment instead of expanding classical-ceiling studies. Finish the cheap objective-mismatch and mode diagnoses. The demand-capped rescore has already stopped because receipts omit the necessary records; capture those records in this experiment. The tiny, partly unsupported C3 pilot does not justify scaling training.

